 "purpose": "The repeat bin (Leitner system) and the mastery status per skill.",
 "details": "A wrong topic enters bin 1 and returns tomorrow; each correct repeat moves it to bin 2 (after 3 days) and bin 3 (after 7 days), and a correct answer after bin 3 removes it. A wrong repeat starts again in bin 1. Repeating always uses new numbers so the child learns the rule, not the answer. Mastery: at least 10 answers and at least 80 percent of the last 20 correct; a mastered skill not practised for 14 days becomes 'fris houden' (keep fresh). Storage goes through Opslag.",
 "module_docstring": "De herhaalbak (Leitner-systeem) en de beheersing per vaardigheid.",
